     3,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:Verdana;font-size:12.0px\"><div><div><div name=\"quote\" style=\"margin:10px 5px 5px 10px;padding:10px 0 10px 10px;border-left:2px solid #c3d9e5;word-wrap:break-word\"><div name=\"quoted-content\"><div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Dear Josh,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">as a minimum, you could take the published code for Bayesian analysis using JAGS from R from our BPA and AHM1 books, see here:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><span>-<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">          </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><a href=\"https://www.vogelwarte.ch/de/projekte/publikationen/bpa/code-for-running-bpa-using-jags\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.vogelwarte.ch/de/projekte/publikationen/bpa/code-for-running-bpa-using-jags&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450449167000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07phmQe2WEjfFFIEP8EdJZ\">https://www.vogelwarte.ch/de/projekte/publikationen/bpa/code-for-running-bpa-using-jags</a>. Here, we still use R2jags, but doing it in jagsUI (our current preference for an R-JAGS interface) is really easy if you have code for R2jags.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><span>-<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">          </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><a href=\"https://www.mbr-pwrc.usgs.gov/pubanalysis/keryroylebook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.mbr-pwrc.usgs.gov/pubanalysis/keryroylebook/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450449167000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2y8Jl5UoNME7AU9yccvbaV\">https://www.mbr-pwrc.usgs.gov/pubanalysis/keryroylebook/</a>. Lots of code here.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Best regards  -- Marc</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Tahoma,sans-serif\">Von:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Tahoma,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a>] <b>Im Auftrag von </b>Joshua Hubbell<br>\r\n<b>Gesendet:</b> Dienstag, 4. August 2020 23:06<br>\r\n<b>An:</b> unmarked<br>\r\n<b>Betreff:</b> [unmarked] JAGs examples</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi unmarked users,</p>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;m trying to teach myself how to implement build JAGS models in R and I was curious if anyone knew of any good online</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">resources/tutorials for how to build occupancy and n-mixture models using jagsUI. Thoughts?</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks,</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Josh</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">--<br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;unmarked&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unmarked+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/unmarked/f874176e-bd4e-4c77-a6bd-4167b65f44e1o%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/unmarked/f874176e-bd4e-4c77-a6bd-4167b65f44e1o%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450449168000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2iPbcB1YPvpC0FF-dFY3ke\"> https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/unmarked/f874176e-bd4e-4c77-a6bd-4167b65f44e1o%40googlegroups.com</a>.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n--<br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;unmarked&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unmarked+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
